   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Wood",
   "resumo_en": "Wild Wood is the second solo studio album by English singer-songwriter Paul Weller, released in September 1993. It reached number 2 on the UK Albums Chart and spawned four hit singles: \"Wild Wood\" (peaked at number 14), \"Sunflower\" (reached number 16), \"The Weaver\" (released as \"The Weaver EP\", peaked at number 18) and \"Hung Up\" (reached number 11 on the UK Singles Charts).\nThe original 1993 UK and European CD editions contained 15 tracks. A sixteenth track was added to the US release and the 1994 UK reissue. A two-disc deluxe edition was released on 22 October 2007.\nThe title track, \"Wild Wood\", was released as a single in 1993, with \"Ends of the Earth\" as its B-side. It reached number 14 on the UK charts in September that year.",
